1
00:00:23,272 --> 00:00:24,482
Morning.

2
00:00:25,816 --> 00:00:27,944
Helicopter company. Cool.

3
00:00:28,277 --> 00:00:31,822
I see no yellow tape, no solemn cops.
Why are we here, Lisbon?

4
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:32,990
I don't know, Jane.

5
00:00:33,115 --> 00:00:35,159
All I know is the director
called me at 4:30 a.m.

6
00:00:35,284 --> 00:00:38,287
and asked me to handle this personally,
whatever this is.

7
00:00:38,412 --> 00:00:39,747
And you just do
whatever the director says

8
00:00:39,872 --> 00:00:41,624
- no questions asked?
- Uh, he's the director.

9
00:00:41,749 --> 00:00:44,043
Okay, well, call me
when you figure it out.

10
00:00:44,168 --> 00:00:45,836
Hey. Wait. No, he asked
for you specifically, too.

11
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:50,132
I take this nap for freedom, Lisbon
for every little guy who has a dream.

12
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,385
Nap later.
Now we fight crime.

13
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:54,345
- No. I'm napping now.
- Agent Lisbon.

14
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:56,764
- Mr. Jane.
- Hi.

15
00:00:56,889 --> 00:00:59,600
Garth Drucker, Head of Security
for Mr. Bajoran.

16
00:00:59,892 --> 00:01:02,228
Guess I nap for freedom
a little later.

17
00:01:02,478 --> 00:01:06,274
Our C.E.O. Yuri Bajoran received
a call just after midnight.

18
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:09,652
It was a computerized voice telling him
to put his affairs in order

19
00:01:09,777 --> 00:01:11,862
and that he'd be killed
in the next 24 hours.

20
00:01:12,196 --> 00:01:14,115
Hang on. Wait.
A death threat?

21
00:01:18,327 --> 00:01:19,370
Usually we only get the case

22
00:01:19,495 --> 00:01:21,539
once there's actually
been, uh, a death

23
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:24,000
so your boss, Mr. Bajoran, has
obviously pulled some strings

24
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,167
to get us here.

25
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:29,213
No. No. Mr. Bajoran didn't want
the police. He was adamant.

26
00:01:29,338 --> 00:01:32,883
Well, someone asked for Agent Lisbon
and me specifically

27
00:01:33,342 --> 00:01:35,970
and that someone
must be very powerful

28
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,432
probably very rich, someone like, uh...

29
00:01:43,686 --> 00:01:45,187
Walter Mashburn?

30
00:01:47,565 --> 00:01:51,027
Thank heavens you're here,
Patrick and Agent...

31
00:01:51,193 --> 00:01:53,362
- Lisbon.
- Lisbon. Right.

32
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:54,905
Good to see you.

33
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:56,616
- Did you bring us here?
- I did.

34
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:58,034
Poor Yuri's in danger.

35
00:01:58,159 --> 00:01:59,785
Now I'm acquiring
his company today

36
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:02,538
and I can't have him expire
before he signs the contract.

37
00:02:02,663 --> 00:02:03,706
You know them?

38
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,083
Oh, just a little misunderstanding
last year.

39
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:07,543
For a brief moment, uh

40
00:02:07,668 --> 00:02:10,087
Walter was a murder suspect
in one of our cases.

41
00:02:10,755 --> 00:02:11,964
Didn't do it.

42
00:02:14,842 --> 00:02:17,136
Mr. Mashburn,
we're sworn officers of the law.

43
00:02:17,261 --> 00:02:19,221
We're not your own personal
private investigators.

44
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:21,432
Well, when I heard Yuri
was in trouble

45
00:02:21,557 --> 00:02:24,060
naturally I wanted the best
in law enforcement.

46
00:02:24,393 --> 00:02:26,270
I take the threat against him
very seriously.

47
00:02:26,979 --> 00:02:28,064
Right, Yuri?

48
00:02:28,981 --> 00:02:30,775
Let's sign the contract, Walter.

49
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,818
I wanna start spending
my new fortune.

50
00:02:34,445 --> 00:02:35,946
Yuri Bajoran.

51
00:02:36,572 --> 00:02:39,241
Don't make yourself comfortable.
You won't be here long.

52
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:42,036
I'm Agent Lisbon, Mr. Bajoran.
We're here about the threat.

53
00:02:42,161 --> 00:02:45,247
Forget the threat. It's a prank,
a scam. I'm a wealthy man.

54
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:48,376
- I get threats. End of story.
- No. He's worried.

55
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,253
It's fascinating how
this man can read people.

56
00:02:51,379 --> 00:02:53,589
Like magic, really.
Wish I had the skill.

57
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:55,341
I doubt the insights
of a state employee

58
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:57,301
are all that remarkable.

59
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,011
Let's go, Walter.

60
00:02:59,136 --> 00:03:01,305
Uh, you're former military

61
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:04,350
uh, ex-Special Forces
from some Baltic nation

62
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,894
possibly, uh, former K.G.B.

63
00:03:07,019 --> 00:03:09,355
but in short, you're just
a thug in a rug.

64
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:13,442
- I apologize, sir. He doesn't...
- And despite your impatience

65
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:16,028
the last thing you feel like doing
is this deal, because, uh

66
00:03:16,153 --> 00:03:18,614
you don't like Walter
and Walter doesn't like you.

67
00:03:19,323 --> 00:03:20,658
Is he great or what?

68
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:24,870
You've wasted enough of my time.
Sign the contract now, Walter.

69
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:27,373
Drucker, with me.

70
00:03:27,873 --> 00:03:30,543
Don't be such a baby, Yuri.
I'm sorry.

71
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:34,422
Ah. Looks like I might get that nap sooner
rather than later.

72
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:35,715
Shall we?

73
00:03:36,632 --> 00:03:38,676
Let's do the damn deal, Walter.

74
00:03:40,594 --> 00:03:41,679
Teresa, hey.

75
00:03:42,012 --> 00:03:45,182
While you're here maybe you and I
could get together sometime soon...

76
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:01,323
Lisbon?

77
00:04:07,705 --> 00:04:09,999
Help! Help!

78
00:04:22,009 --> 00:04:23,343
Check on that right now!

79
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,731
Oh, stop it. You're fine.

80
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:37,941
{\an8}- He's fine, right?
- He will be.

81
00:04:38,066 --> 00:04:40,152
{\an8}And that guy's got a pretty
bad laceration, but he'll live.

82
00:04:40,694 --> 00:04:44,490
{\an8}I'll live, Teresa. Did you hear that?
I'm alive. It's fantastic.

83
00:04:44,615 --> 00:04:47,326
{\an8}Yes, it is. Enjoy the adrenaline
while it lasts.

84
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,329
{\an8}Hey, boss. So I spoke
to the arson unit commander.

85
00:04:50,621 --> 00:04:52,498
He said it was a massive
subsonic explosive device

86
00:04:52,623 --> 00:04:54,082
probably C-4 or Semtex.

87
00:04:54,208 --> 00:04:56,835
{\an8}A giant bomb, Rigsby. Just...
just say it's a giant bomb.

88
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:58,420
Yeah, or a giant bomb.

89
00:04:58,545 --> 00:04:59,755
The blast seat was
under the conference table

90
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,256
made a crater
the size of a minivan.

91
00:05:01,882 --> 00:05:04,551
- If I hadn't left when I did, then...
- Yeah, you'd be vaporized, too.

92
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,637
Flirting with Lisbon...
that's what saved him.

93
00:05:06,762 --> 00:05:08,472
- He wasn't flirting with me.
- I wasn't flirting.

94
00:05:10,224 --> 00:05:11,892
{\an8}Any indication
of terrorist involvement?

95
00:05:12,017 --> 00:05:15,270
{\an8}Uh, no. It was a very specific,
targeted detonation.

96
00:05:15,521 --> 00:05:17,689
{\an8}- To kill Yuri.
- Yeah, and they succeeded.

97
00:05:17,856 --> 00:05:19,483
{\an8}Forensics found
enough remains...barely...

98
00:05:19,608 --> 00:05:21,318
{\an8}to identify Bajoran
and his Head of Security.

99
00:05:21,610 --> 00:05:23,153
{\an8}Drucker. Poor guy.

100
00:05:23,695 --> 00:05:25,572
{\an8}I told Yuri we should move
the meeting to my office

101
00:05:25,697 --> 00:05:28,283
{\an8}but he flat-out refused.
Stubborn old bull.

102
00:05:28,534 --> 00:05:29,701
{\an8}Someone threatens Yuri

103
00:05:29,827 --> 00:05:31,662
{\an8}wanting to frighten him
before killing him.

104
00:05:31,995 --> 00:05:33,038
Who hated him that much?

105
00:05:33,163 --> 00:05:34,331
{\an8}Oh! Oh! I know that one.

106
00:05:37,876 --> 00:05:38,919
{\an8}Huh?

107
00:05:42,798 --> 00:05:45,759
{\an8}If I killed him, Teresa,
why would I call in the CBI?

108
00:05:45,926 --> 00:05:48,637
{\an8}You like games, thrills,
Mr. Mashburn.

109
00:05:49,263 --> 00:05:52,766
{\an8}Walter, please.
Mr. Mashburn was my mother.

110
00:05:53,892 --> 00:05:55,060
{\an8}I almost died myself.

111
00:05:55,185 --> 00:05:57,020
{\an8}Yeah, but you escaped
at the very last moment.

112
00:05:57,145 --> 00:05:58,188
{\an8}That was lucky.

113
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,523
{\an8}True.

114
00:06:00,649 --> 00:06:02,484
{\an8}I guess I do look suspicious.

115
00:06:03,151 --> 00:06:04,194
{\an8}Sit down.

116
00:06:06,905 --> 00:06:09,867
{\an8}Don't take this personally.
I have to ask these questions.

117
00:06:12,119 --> 00:06:14,913
{\an8}Do you have the knowledge
and the resources to build a bomb?

118
00:06:16,832 --> 00:06:19,626
{\an8}Yes. But you know that already,
don't you?

119
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:24,756
My first company, Mashburn Avionics
made high-tech weaponry.

120
00:06:24,965 --> 00:06:28,927
But I started out with cherry bombs
in the toilets at reform school.

121
00:06:29,136 --> 00:06:30,429
You went to reform school?

122
00:06:30,929 --> 00:06:33,015
My teachers thought
I was incorrigible.

123
00:06:34,224 --> 00:06:35,893
But you know that, too.

124
00:06:36,727 --> 00:06:38,729
Have you ever visited
Bajoran's Helicopter Plant

125
00:06:38,854 --> 00:06:40,480
or solicited anybody
to go there?

126
00:06:40,606 --> 00:06:41,857
You mean, to plant a bomb?

127
00:06:43,233 --> 00:06:44,818
No, ma'am. Never have.

128
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:47,821
The threat to Yuri Bajoran was made
from a disposable phone

129
00:06:47,946 --> 00:06:50,157
that was purchased
at a drugstore in Marin County.

130
00:06:50,324 --> 00:06:51,491
Where I have a place...

131
00:06:52,326 --> 00:06:54,536
Along with 250,000 other people.

132
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,748
Look, Teresa,
I didn't need to kill Yuri.

133
00:06:57,998 --> 00:07:00,834
I'd already done worse.
I destroyed him.

134
00:07:00,959 --> 00:07:03,545
- By taking over his company?
- His flagship.

135
00:07:03,921 --> 00:07:05,756
Yuri and I had been
at each other for years

136
00:07:05,881 --> 00:07:08,425
and I had finally won.
Don't you see?

137
00:07:08,550 --> 00:07:11,094
I'd forced him
to sell me his baby.

138
00:07:11,219 --> 00:07:13,722
Although he died before
he signed the contract.

139
00:07:13,847 --> 00:07:15,933
I know. The bastard.

140
00:07:16,058 --> 00:07:19,311
It's like he reached out from the grave
to deny me one last time.

141
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:22,314
But bottom line... I beat him

142
00:07:23,231 --> 00:07:26,401
and I wanted him waking up for the next
30 years thinking about that.

143
00:07:26,902 --> 00:07:29,404
You hated him so much
you wanted him alive?

144
00:07:29,529 --> 00:07:33,158
Exactly.
Yuri Bajoran was a bad man, Teresa.

145
00:07:33,492 --> 00:07:34,868
So who wanted him dead?

146
00:07:34,993 --> 00:07:37,579
Who didn't? Aside from me.

147
00:07:38,121 --> 00:07:39,331
His widow?

148
00:07:39,498 --> 00:07:42,709
Marie? No. Fair point.

149
00:07:43,502 --> 00:07:45,462
She seemed to love him
for some reason.

150
00:07:45,587 --> 00:07:46,755
You know her?

151
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:51,385
I was engaged to her, actually,
years back.

152
00:07:52,386 --> 00:07:54,262
She married Yuri instead.

153
00:07:55,931 --> 00:07:57,224
Great lady.

154
00:07:57,349 --> 00:08:00,477
Despite that tragic lapse
in judgment, a great lady.

155
00:08:00,769 --> 00:08:02,145
How was the marriage?

156
00:08:03,814 --> 00:08:04,940
Oh, you'd have to ask her.

157
00:08:05,065 --> 00:08:08,652
So, Teresa, I'm tired of doing
this whole suspect thing again.

158
00:08:08,777 --> 00:08:09,820
Not fun at all.

159
00:08:09,945 --> 00:08:13,615
How about I play Detective this time
give you and Patrick a hand?

160
00:08:13,824 --> 00:08:16,243
- Not a chance.
- Oh, never say "never."

161
00:08:16,368 --> 00:08:18,495
Never, Walter. Never ever.

162
00:08:22,833 --> 00:08:24,001
That's a maybe.

163
00:08:27,838 --> 00:08:31,675
{\an8}So you were engaged to Walter Mashburn
before you married Yuri?

164
00:08:32,551 --> 00:08:35,262
That was years ago.
Why would you ask that?

165
00:08:35,387 --> 00:08:37,014
Oh, nosy.

166
00:08:37,139 --> 00:08:39,558
Did you dump him
or did he dump you? And why?

167
00:08:40,976 --> 00:08:42,269
It's none of your business.

168
00:08:44,938 --> 00:08:47,649
I fell in love with Yuri
is all I'll say.

169
00:08:49,276 --> 00:08:52,612
I know what people said about him
but they were wrong.

170
00:08:54,156 --> 00:08:56,992
He was a wonderful, loving person.

171
00:09:00,787 --> 00:09:02,706
Interesting woman.
Didn't kill Yuri.

172
00:09:02,873 --> 00:09:04,833
Um, I'm sorry.
Where's the bathroom?

173
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:07,377
- This way.
- Thank you.

174
00:09:07,627 --> 00:09:08,837
Sorry for your loss.

175
00:09:13,467 --> 00:09:15,552
- Who is that man?
- It's a long story.

176
00:09:16,094 --> 00:09:18,847
Now, Mrs. Bajoran, who would
want your husband dead?

177
00:09:18,972 --> 00:09:20,682
Yuri was a powerful man.

178
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,310
Powerful men have enemies.

179
00:10:46,226 --> 00:10:47,519
This takeover by Mashburn...

180
00:10:47,644 --> 00:10:49,187
is it true your husband
didn't want to sell?

181
00:10:49,312 --> 00:10:52,315
Walter tricked him.
It wasn't right.

182
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,483
Tricked him how?

183
00:10:53,608 --> 00:10:55,569
He approached someone
Yuri thought was a friend

184
00:10:55,694 --> 00:10:58,029
and got him to secretly
buy up enough shares

185
00:10:58,155 --> 00:11:00,031
so that Walter could force
the takeover.

186
00:11:00,365 --> 00:11:02,367
- Name?
- Markham Shankar

187
00:11:02,993 --> 00:11:04,536
software mogul.

188
00:11:04,911 --> 00:11:07,330
Turns out he'd secretly
hated Yuri for years

189
00:11:07,455 --> 00:11:11,084
some ridiculous business dispute
he wouldn't forgive.

190
00:11:13,086 --> 00:11:15,839
Ma'am, you have a lovely home.
It's very, uh, cozy.

191
00:11:15,964 --> 00:11:19,342
Thanks for having us.
Cho, we should... go.

192
00:11:20,635 --> 00:11:21,678
Thank you.

193
00:11:26,808 --> 00:11:28,435
Been a pleasure.
Thank you.

194
00:11:36,109 --> 00:11:37,944
According to the Marin D.A.'s Office

195
00:11:38,069 --> 00:11:40,780
Markham Shankar had good reason
to hate Bajoran.

196
00:11:41,198 --> 00:11:44,201
Six years ago, he claimed Bajoran
cheated him out of a couple million bucks

197
00:11:44,326 --> 00:11:46,995
he even tried to get the D.A.'s office
to file fraud charges.

198
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,163
Did you talk to him yet?

199
00:11:48,288 --> 00:11:51,958
I can't even find him. No one's
photographed Shankar since 2002.

200
00:11:52,167 --> 00:11:53,335
The guy's a recluse.

201
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:55,295
His office won't even admit
he's in the country.

202
00:11:55,670 --> 00:11:57,088
Keep looking into it.

203
00:11:58,131 --> 00:12:00,425
- And you...
- Hello, Lisbon.

204
00:12:01,176 --> 00:12:03,345
What a great day
to not be blown up.

205
00:12:03,470 --> 00:12:05,680
- Give it up now.
- Give what up?

206
00:12:06,014 --> 00:12:07,807
What you took
from Bajoran's house.

207
00:12:10,018 --> 00:12:12,395
The toupee, Jane.
The housekeeper called.

208
00:12:20,528 --> 00:12:22,322
That's just gross.
Why would you take it?

209
00:12:22,489 --> 00:12:23,907
- Evidence.
- Of what?

210
00:12:24,574 --> 00:12:25,825
Bad taste.

211
00:12:26,117 --> 00:12:27,452
Let me explain something.

212
00:12:27,577 --> 00:12:29,621
You do not mess
with super-rich people.

213
00:12:29,746 --> 00:12:31,206
They're like kids
with machine guns.

214
00:12:31,331 --> 00:12:33,583
- Super-rich people, like Mashburn?
- What about Mashburn?

215
00:12:33,708 --> 00:12:36,294
Oh, my God. You're just
so obsessed with Mashburn.

216
00:12:36,419 --> 00:12:39,214
- You're the one who brought him up.
- What is it with you and him?

217
00:12:39,339 --> 00:12:42,259
Got something. Whenever Shankar
is in San Francisco

218
00:12:42,384 --> 00:12:44,219
he likes to stay
at Chaparral Glen.

219
00:12:45,011 --> 00:12:46,554
- What's that?
- Country Club.

220
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,515
The most exclusive in California.

221
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,058
It's 100 grand to join.

222
00:12:50,183 --> 00:12:53,019
They've got a 2,300-acre campus
in the woods.

223
00:12:53,186 --> 00:12:55,105
Shankar likes "glamping."

224
00:12:57,983 --> 00:12:59,526
You know, glamorous camping?

225
00:12:59,651 --> 00:13:01,528
- You made that up.
- Did not.

226
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:03,905
Glamping... I like it.

227
00:13:04,197 --> 00:13:06,616
Lisbon, shall we go and talk
to some more super-rich people?

228
00:13:06,866 --> 00:13:07,993
Do something with that.

229
00:13:14,833 --> 00:13:17,419
{\an8}I'm sorry, Agent, but I can't tell you
if Mr. Shankar is here

230
00:13:17,544 --> 00:13:20,005
{\an8}and unless you have a search warrant
I can't allow you on the grounds.

231
00:13:20,297 --> 00:13:22,007
Our members are quite concerned
about privacy.

232
00:13:22,132 --> 00:13:24,217
I'm concerned about
a double homicide, sir.

233
00:13:24,342 --> 00:13:27,887
- Hey, Walter.
- Hey, Patrick. Teresa.

234
00:13:28,013 --> 00:13:30,348
Walter's a member here.
I thought we might need his help.

235
00:13:30,473 --> 00:13:31,516
Mr. Trevayne

236
00:13:31,641 --> 00:13:33,893
my friends Patrick and Teresa
will be joining us here today.

237
00:13:34,019 --> 00:13:36,521
Sir, that won't be necessary.
We have your card on file.

238
00:13:37,147 --> 00:13:38,606
What's the limit on that thing?

239
00:13:38,982 --> 00:13:40,025
I don't know if there is one.

240
00:13:40,275 --> 00:13:42,277
- Go find old Shankar, then?
- Let's.

241
00:13:43,528 --> 00:13:45,071
Never say "never."

242
00:13:45,864 --> 00:13:48,283
You know, Shankar's campsite
is right up on that ridge over there.

243
00:13:48,450 --> 00:13:49,909
You can see the whole valley
from there.

244
00:13:51,453 --> 00:13:53,496
This campsite... you want it.
You wish you owned it.

245
00:13:53,621 --> 00:13:56,333
- I do. How'd you know?
- Pupil dilation.

246
00:13:56,458 --> 00:13:57,584
- Pupil dilation?
- Yes.

247
00:13:57,709 --> 00:14:00,045
When someone sees something they want
their pupils dilate.

248
00:14:01,004 --> 00:14:02,380
Pupil dilation.

249
00:14:06,217 --> 00:14:08,136
- Fantastic.
- Yes, it is.

250
00:14:15,977 --> 00:14:17,020
Thank you.

251
00:14:19,147 --> 00:14:20,690
Tell us about Markham Shankar.

252
00:14:20,815 --> 00:14:22,484
Is he still mad at Yuri
about the fraud?

253
00:14:22,609 --> 00:14:24,611
Oh, you bet.
Angry guy... Markham.

254
00:14:25,028 --> 00:14:28,281
When I offered him the right incentive
he was very happy to betray Yuri.

255
00:14:28,406 --> 00:14:31,785
What incentive can you offer a rich man
that he can't buy for himself?

256
00:14:31,951 --> 00:14:34,287
A propeller from a
Beech Bonanza airplane.

257
00:14:34,621 --> 00:14:35,663
Come again?

258
00:14:35,789 --> 00:14:38,500
It was the only remaining piece
of the plane Buddy Holly died in.

259
00:14:38,666 --> 00:14:40,460
Markham's obsessed
with celebrity deaths

260
00:14:40,585 --> 00:14:42,420
has a huge collection
of death memorabilia.

261
00:14:42,545 --> 00:14:45,382
- How intriguingly creepy.
- Ah, poor Markham's bored.

262
00:14:45,965 --> 00:14:47,300
What about you, Walter?

263
00:14:47,425 --> 00:14:49,636
Last year, you said
you'd do anything for a thrill.

264
00:14:50,512 --> 00:14:51,554
What do you have in mind?

265
00:14:51,805 --> 00:14:52,931
Get down!

266
00:15:02,065 --> 00:15:03,525
Thrilling enough for you, Walter?

267
00:15:10,988 --> 00:15:13,366
- You guys okay?
- I'm fine. Thanks.

268
00:15:13,825 --> 00:15:16,869
We're fine. Shankar might be mad
at Mashburn and Yuri.

269
00:15:16,994 --> 00:15:19,288
- Did you find him?
- Nope. No sign at Shankar's cabin.

270
00:15:19,414 --> 00:15:21,165
The place is like
Buckingham Palace, by the way.

271
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:22,500
And we searched
all over those woods.

272
00:15:22,625 --> 00:15:23,876
Even the dogs
couldn't pick up a trail.

273
00:15:24,127 --> 00:15:25,503
Have you guys ever been
to an auction?

274
00:15:25,795 --> 00:15:29,257
What? I'm gonna call immigration
see if Shankar's left the country.

275
00:15:29,382 --> 00:15:32,093
Yeah, and see where he parks his boat
or his plane or whatever.

276
00:15:32,218 --> 00:15:33,428
But, boss, he's got no record

277
00:15:33,553 --> 00:15:35,680
and we didn't see anything in that cabin
that would tie him to this...

278
00:15:35,805 --> 00:15:38,641
no gun, ammo, nothing.
Maybe he was never there at all.

279
00:15:38,808 --> 00:15:40,810
And why would he wanna kill
both Yuri and Mashburn?

280
00:15:40,977 --> 00:15:44,355
He doesn't. Actually,
no one wanted to kill Yuri.

281
00:15:44,522 --> 00:15:45,565
What are you talking about?

282
00:15:45,690 --> 00:15:48,025
What if Walter were
the intended target all along?

283
00:15:48,151 --> 00:15:51,320
I mean, he was supposed to die
in that explosion but he didn't.

284
00:15:51,696 --> 00:15:54,615
So the killer follows him
to Chaparral Glen to finish the job.

285
00:15:54,782 --> 00:15:56,951
But the death threat...
it was against Yuri.

286
00:15:57,076 --> 00:15:59,078
Ah, yes, very clever.

287
00:15:59,245 --> 00:16:02,540
Completely threw all of us...
well, almost all of us.

288
00:16:04,375 --> 00:16:05,585
Sorry, Walter.

289
00:16:06,669 --> 00:16:07,712
I have a favor.

290
00:16:07,837 --> 00:16:09,630
Could I borrow that, uh, fancy
little credit card of yours?

291
00:16:09,922 --> 00:16:12,592
Uh, yeah, yeah. What for?

292
00:16:12,717 --> 00:16:14,635
I thought I'd find Shankar.
Thank you.

293
00:16:16,512 --> 00:16:17,555
What's going on?

294
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:20,224
Did Markham Shankar have
a reason to be angry with you?

295
00:16:23,811 --> 00:16:25,146
Walter.

296
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,484
The takeover
of Yuri's company...

297
00:16:30,359 --> 00:16:32,695
Markham may have been under
the mistaken impression

298
00:16:32,862 --> 00:16:34,989
that he'd receive shares
in return for his help.

299
00:16:35,114 --> 00:16:37,450
But if it was him, wouldn't he
have hired better assassins?

300
00:16:37,909 --> 00:16:40,411
Okay, is there anybody else
who might wanna kill you?

301
00:16:40,786 --> 00:16:42,830
I have lots of enemies, Teresa.

302
00:16:43,873 --> 00:16:47,335
You'd be surprised to hear this
but some people find me annoying.

303
00:16:51,297 --> 00:16:54,383
Yes... My pupils are dilated.

304
00:16:56,052 --> 00:16:57,595
That's not what I was wondering.

305
00:16:58,763 --> 00:16:59,889
Fair enough.

306
00:17:00,598 --> 00:17:03,559
Look, I'll give you a list
of all my nonfriends

307
00:17:03,684 --> 00:17:06,229
but none of them has the stones
to kill me, I promise you.

308
00:17:06,354 --> 00:17:08,940
We'll look into your phone records
and see if anything else comes up.

309
00:17:12,401 --> 00:17:13,444
- Teresa.
- What?

310
00:17:13,569 --> 00:17:15,279
No. You have a...

311
00:17:18,157 --> 00:17:19,575
It's a bullet hole.

312
00:17:20,993 --> 00:17:24,080
It was close. Really close.

313
00:17:29,126 --> 00:17:31,337
Usually, I can buy my way
out of trouble.

314
00:17:32,463 --> 00:17:33,923
Ask my ex-wives.

315
00:17:39,512 --> 00:17:41,597
Don't worry.
We'll keep you safe.

316
00:17:42,139 --> 00:17:44,392
It's procedure to assign
an Agent to protect you.

317
00:17:44,517 --> 00:17:46,561
Oh. Excellent.

318
00:17:46,686 --> 00:17:49,647
- Agent Cho will be here shortly.
- Chicken.

319
00:18:11,669 --> 00:18:13,170
Hello and welcome to Ogilvy.

320
00:18:13,296 --> 00:18:18,301
The auction begins with lot one
a full suit of 16th-century jousting armor.

321
00:18:18,467 --> 00:18:22,638
Let's start the bidding at $30,000.
Do I hear $30,000?

322
00:18:22,888 --> 00:18:25,516
And $30,000's bid off to my left.
Yes, and $31,000.

323
00:18:25,641 --> 00:18:28,185
$31,000. Go $32,000. Thank you.
$32,000 on the right there.

324
00:18:28,311 --> 00:18:30,521
$32,000. Go $33,000. The new bid
at $33,000, at $34,000.

325
00:18:30,646 --> 00:18:32,481
Bid's all the way to $34,000 with the lady
in the front there

326
00:18:32,607 --> 00:18:34,275
$34,000. Go $35,000 if you wish.

327
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,861
$35,000 is bid. $36,000.
New bid at $36,000.

328
00:18:36,986 --> 00:18:38,904
Do I hear $37,000?

329
00:18:43,618 --> 00:18:46,329
Oh, hey, boss.
Markham Shankar has a yacht.

330
00:18:46,454 --> 00:18:48,581
Coast Guard says he sails
tonight, leaving the country.

331
00:18:48,706 --> 00:18:49,749
Camp out on the dock.

332
00:18:49,874 --> 00:18:51,542
Do not leave
until you've questioned Shankar.

333
00:18:51,667 --> 00:18:52,710
Yeah, you got it.

334
00:18:52,835 --> 00:18:55,046
A possible suspect
Mashburn forgot to mention...

335
00:18:55,171 --> 00:18:57,048
his ex-girlfriend, Elsa Struven.

336
00:18:58,299 --> 00:18:59,342
When did they break up?

337
00:18:59,467 --> 00:19:02,345
Two months ago. And apparently,
she wasn't very happy about it.

338
00:19:02,553 --> 00:19:05,014
According to reports, she
threatened him with violence.

339
00:19:05,139 --> 00:19:06,682
Reports?
He filed a complaint?

340
00:19:07,266 --> 00:19:11,354
Uh, no. Published reports,
in the media.

341
00:19:12,396 --> 00:19:13,898
Okay, the tabloids.

342
00:19:14,023 --> 00:19:15,358
She's a German supermodel.

343
00:19:18,903 --> 00:19:20,446
Of course she is.

344
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:22,990
- Talk to her.
- Okay.

345
00:19:25,993 --> 00:19:27,244
Supermodel.

346
00:19:27,745 --> 00:19:30,122
{\an8}If I have to do an L.B.O.,
I will, Denise.

347
00:19:30,873 --> 00:19:33,209
{\an8}But all that debt?
It could crush you.

348
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:36,253
I'll tell you what.

349
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:39,715
I'm willing to pay an extra eighth a share
if we ink it by month's end.

350
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:41,133
Just think about it.

351
00:19:42,551 --> 00:19:45,304
Okay.
Love to Larry and the kids.

352
00:19:47,890 --> 00:19:49,016
You do a lot of business
on the phone?

353
00:19:49,141 --> 00:19:50,309
I do a lot of business.

354
00:19:50,518 --> 00:19:52,687
Phone, texts, e-mails...
doesn't really matter.

355
00:19:53,604 --> 00:19:55,022
Threats work better
on the phone.

356
00:19:55,356 --> 00:19:58,150
That wasn't a threat, Agent Cho.
That was a negotiation.

357
00:20:00,611 --> 00:20:03,531
Hey, I know. We could go to the track
race bikes for a couple of hours.

358
00:20:04,323 --> 00:20:06,242
- Motorcycles?
- Yes.

359
00:20:07,535 --> 00:20:08,744
No. Too exposed.

360
00:20:08,869 --> 00:20:10,579
Okay, then we'll take the Lambo
out for a spin.

361
00:20:10,705 --> 00:20:11,747
It's not safe.

362
00:20:11,872 --> 00:20:13,874
- It has air bags.
- Is it bulletproof?

363
00:20:13,999 --> 00:20:15,459
Can I at least
shoot your gun then?

364
00:20:19,004 --> 00:20:22,007
Patrick. Thank God.

365
00:20:22,133 --> 00:20:25,845
What are the chances of you putting
a party together in, uh... five hours?

366
00:20:26,053 --> 00:20:28,013
Mm... could do, sure.

367
00:20:28,764 --> 00:20:30,516
Sounds fun.

368
00:20:31,308 --> 00:20:32,351
"Invite all of your friends."

369
00:20:32,476 --> 00:20:33,519
I mean, really get
the word out there

370
00:20:33,644 --> 00:20:35,730
'cause you're celebrating, Walter.
You're celebrating.

371
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,815
I am? Great.
Celebrating what?

372
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:39,525
Oh, uh, I gotta go. Gotta go.

373
00:20:39,650 --> 00:20:42,820
- Uh, uh, $90,000?
- That's $90,000 for lot 10.

374
00:20:42,987 --> 00:20:44,947
And I see $100,000
from the woman in red.

375
00:20:45,322 --> 00:20:47,575
$110,000? Do I hear $110,000?
$110,000 and $120,000?

376
00:20:47,908 --> 00:20:50,327
- $120,000. Thank you. $120,000.
- Uh, $150,000.

377
00:20:50,870 --> 00:20:51,912
Never was any good at math.

378
00:20:52,037 --> 00:20:53,622
I've got $150,000 from
the gentleman in the vest.

379
00:20:53,748 --> 00:20:57,710
How about $160,000? $160,000.
$160,000 is bid.

380
00:20:57,835 --> 00:20:59,962
How about $170,000?
I've got $170,000 and $180,000.

381
00:21:00,129 --> 00:21:02,131
And the gentleman in the front
row, $180,000 is your bid, sir.

382
00:21:02,256 --> 00:21:03,674
You've got the bid at $180,000.
$190,000?

383
00:21:03,841 --> 00:21:05,760
Can we move this thing along?
$200,000.

384
00:21:06,135 --> 00:21:08,512
And $200,000 from our
enthusiastic friend in the back.

385
00:21:08,637 --> 00:21:09,847
Do I hear $210,000?

386
00:21:09,972 --> 00:21:11,223
- Nice day for it, huh?
- Ah, yes.

387
00:21:12,266 --> 00:21:13,893
And whose interests
do you represent?

388
00:21:14,018 --> 00:21:15,853
Well, that's supposed to be
confidential, isn't it?

389
00:21:15,978 --> 00:21:17,605
But what the heck?
Walter Mashburn.

390
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,607
$230,000 if you wish, sir.
$230,000?

391
00:21:19,732 --> 00:21:23,360
$230,000. $230,000.
Do we have $240,000?

392
00:21:23,486 --> 00:21:24,570
- Uh, sir...
- $240,000.

393
00:21:24,695 --> 00:21:25,738
Do we have $240,000?

394
00:21:25,863 --> 00:21:26,906
- $240,000.
- $240,000.

395
00:21:27,031 --> 00:21:29,158
We have $240,000 right here.
And we also have $250,000.

396
00:21:29,283 --> 00:21:31,494
I know that because I am bidding it.
Do we have $260,000?

397
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:32,953
- Do we have $260,000, anyone?
- Wait a minute. Wait, wait, wait.

398
00:21:33,078 --> 00:21:35,664
Come on, man, you can do
$260,000. I know you can.

399
00:21:35,790 --> 00:21:36,832
Uh, sir?

400
00:21:36,957 --> 00:21:38,000
Let's go.
What about you, sir?

401
00:21:38,125 --> 00:21:39,168
We have $250,000.

402
00:21:39,293 --> 00:21:41,295
No. I want the thing for
$260,000. Can I have it?

403
00:21:41,754 --> 00:21:42,922
- Yes.
- Thank you.

404
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:54,183
Hey, boss.

405
00:21:55,726 --> 00:21:57,102
- Hi.
- I got something.

406
00:21:57,311 --> 00:21:59,688
Uh, so I go to
the ex-girlfriend's penthouse.

407
00:21:59,814 --> 00:22:01,690
She's not there,
but the roommate lets me in

408
00:22:01,816 --> 00:22:03,526
and I find this
on the bedroom wall.

409
00:22:06,987 --> 00:22:09,073
Elsa. Yikes.

410
00:22:09,198 --> 00:22:10,741
Yep. She's for real.

411
00:22:11,492 --> 00:22:13,452
Mashburn called the police
to his house twice

412
00:22:13,577 --> 00:22:14,870
to break up fights between them.

413
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:17,706
I asked him point-blank

414
00:22:17,832 --> 00:22:19,875
if there was anybody else
who might wanna hurt him.

415
00:22:20,459 --> 00:22:21,710
Why didn't he mention her?

416
00:22:30,427 --> 00:22:31,470
Thank you.

417
00:22:38,936 --> 00:22:41,480
- Sir?
- Oh, please. Thank you.

418
00:22:41,605 --> 00:22:42,648
You're welcome!

419
00:22:46,527 --> 00:22:47,736
What's going on?

420
00:22:47,862 --> 00:22:49,989
It's called a party.
Perhaps you've heard of them.

421
00:22:50,239 --> 00:22:53,409
- You should get yourself a drink.
- I need to talk to Mashburn.

422
00:22:54,076 --> 00:22:56,745
It's here. It looks great,
don't you think?

423
00:22:56,912 --> 00:22:58,706
You still need to speak
to Markham Shankar?

424
00:22:58,831 --> 00:23:01,417
Yeah, Rigsby says he's nowhere
to be found on his yacht. Why?

425
00:23:01,584 --> 00:23:02,626
No reason.

426
00:23:02,751 --> 00:23:05,087
- Teresa, my heroine.
- I need to talk to you.

427
00:23:05,212 --> 00:23:08,424
This woman saved my life,
nearly took a bullet for me.

428
00:23:11,427 --> 00:23:12,595
What the hell is that?

429
00:23:12,803 --> 00:23:14,471
Oh, that's, uh, fragments

430
00:23:14,597 --> 00:23:17,808
of the Porsche Spyder
James Dean died in.

431
00:23:18,017 --> 00:23:20,102
Congratulations, Walter.
You're the owner.

432
00:23:20,644 --> 00:23:21,979
Walter, you son of a bitch.

433
00:23:22,146 --> 00:23:24,315
You outbid me and now you're flaunting it?
You bastard.

434
00:23:24,481 --> 00:23:26,817
- Please step back.
- Meet Markham Shankar.

435
00:23:26,984 --> 00:23:29,612
Uh, I apologize. My bad.
I really needed to talk to you

436
00:23:29,737 --> 00:23:31,322
and you're a very hard man
to track down.

437
00:23:31,697 --> 00:23:33,991
- You lured me here?
- Yeah. Pretty good.

438
00:23:34,533 --> 00:23:35,784
Who the devil
do you think you are?

439
00:23:35,910 --> 00:23:37,411
- The police.
- Cho, you talk to Shankar.

440
00:23:37,536 --> 00:23:39,830
- I've got Mashburn.
- Shankar, did you pull that stunt...

441
00:23:39,997 --> 00:23:41,415
Ladies and gentlemen,
quick announcement...

442
00:23:41,540 --> 00:23:43,125
I'd like you to give
a very warm welcome

443
00:23:43,250 --> 00:23:46,670
to Walter's new girlfriend
number one...Teresa Lisbon!

444
00:23:48,130 --> 00:23:49,882
Hi, Teresa.

445
00:23:51,050 --> 00:23:53,302
- Hi.
- Hi. Nice to meet you.

446
00:23:53,427 --> 00:23:55,429
- Oh, I'm gonna kill him.
- Hi.

447
00:23:56,055 --> 00:23:59,141
- Nice to meet you.
- You, too. Hi.

448
00:23:59,266 --> 00:24:02,019
- Sir, we just have a few questions.
- Yes, we certainly do.

449
00:24:03,395 --> 00:24:04,855
Marie Bajoran...

450
00:24:05,606 --> 00:24:07,024
what's her favorite color?

451
00:24:08,776 --> 00:24:11,779
- Now how would I know that?
- Mr. Shankar, do you own a rifle?

452
00:24:12,029 --> 00:24:13,656
I heard about
the attack on Walter.

453
00:24:13,781 --> 00:24:16,867
It was a terrible thing. So hard
to find a good club these days.

454
00:24:17,451 --> 00:24:20,120
And, yes, I do own several rifles.
What of it?

455
00:24:20,496 --> 00:24:23,874
If I were to kill him I'd do the civilized
thing and hire a professional.

456
00:24:24,166 --> 00:24:25,584
What kind of music
does she like?

457
00:24:26,502 --> 00:24:27,920
I have no idea.

458
00:24:28,045 --> 00:24:29,296
Did you believe Mr. Mashburn
cheated you

459
00:24:29,421 --> 00:24:31,382
in the takeover
of Yuri Bajoran's company?

460
00:24:31,507 --> 00:24:35,386
Yes, but helping to destroy Yuri
was its own reward.

461
00:24:35,761 --> 00:24:36,804
Anything else?

462
00:24:36,929 --> 00:24:38,889
Did she prefer Chinese
or Italian for dinner?

463
00:24:39,014 --> 00:24:40,641
Me, personally... Kung Pao chicken.

464
00:24:40,891 --> 00:24:44,353
Although, I do like a sweet corn ravioli
with a white wine sauce. Very nice.

465
00:24:44,979 --> 00:24:46,897
Is this man on medication, perhaps?

466
00:24:47,022 --> 00:24:49,483
No, I'm not. You weren't
having an affair with her?

467
00:24:50,484 --> 00:24:52,569
Ah. Yes, I see.

468
00:24:53,112 --> 00:24:55,239
Now why would you not
simply ask that to begin with?

469
00:24:55,572 --> 00:24:56,615
Fun.

470
00:24:57,324 --> 00:25:00,494
The answer is no. I do enjoy
seducing other men's wives

471
00:25:00,619 --> 00:25:02,454
but Marie and Yuri
were madly in love.

472
00:25:02,663 --> 00:25:05,457
Not exactly a target with
much potential, now is it?

473
00:25:07,167 --> 00:25:08,210
No.

474
00:25:09,503 --> 00:25:10,754
Yes. Thank you.

475
00:25:10,879 --> 00:25:14,174
Uh, Cho, all this talk of food...
I'll be at the oyster bar.

476
00:25:16,969 --> 00:25:19,638
Mr. Shankar, where were you yesterday
between 3:00 and 5:00 p.m.?

477
00:25:23,308 --> 00:25:24,810
- Drink?
- No.

478
00:25:24,935 --> 00:25:26,937
So my friends say
because you saved my life

479
00:25:27,062 --> 00:25:28,230
that means you own me.

480
00:25:29,023 --> 00:25:30,649
They have a return policy?

481
00:25:30,899 --> 00:25:33,861
Oh, come on. Why so cranky
on such a beautiful night?

482
00:25:33,986 --> 00:25:36,488
Well, Walter,
remember when I asked you

483
00:25:36,613 --> 00:25:38,323
if there was anyone
who wanted you dead

484
00:25:38,449 --> 00:25:40,659
anyone else who might have
been mad at you?

485
00:25:42,202 --> 00:25:45,831
- Elsa Struven, maybe?
- Elsa? Oh, yeah, she was mad.

486
00:25:45,956 --> 00:25:47,166
Why didn't you tell me?

487
00:25:47,374 --> 00:25:48,834
Well, it's not exactly
breaking news.

488
00:25:48,959 --> 00:25:50,836
My girlfriends are all mad
by the time we break up.

489
00:25:51,211 --> 00:25:52,713
I can't imagine why.

490
00:25:53,589 --> 00:25:56,175
Hey. You have to be nice to me.

491
00:25:56,550 --> 00:25:57,843
No, I don't.

492
00:25:58,010 --> 00:26:00,512
I'm a citizen.
You're a public servant.

493
00:26:00,637 --> 00:26:01,930
I'm off duty now.

494
00:26:03,474 --> 00:26:04,725
I upset you, don't I?

495
00:26:04,850 --> 00:26:08,687
Upset me? No.
Irritate me a little? Maybe.

496
00:26:08,812 --> 00:26:09,855
Why?

497
00:26:10,272 --> 00:26:12,524
You're egotistical.
You're arrogant.

498
00:26:12,649 --> 00:26:15,027
You're entitled and rich.

499
00:26:15,277 --> 00:26:17,029
When do we get
to the bad stuff?

500
00:26:19,406 --> 00:26:22,076
- Walter, no!
- Elsa, what are you, nuts?

501
00:26:31,001 --> 00:26:33,045
- I guess this means we're even.
- Yeah.

502
00:26:34,088 --> 00:26:36,965
Uh, enough.
Elsa, calm down.

503
00:26:37,674 --> 00:26:39,093
Some people never change.

504
00:26:51,269 --> 00:26:52,729
Modeling pays well, Elsa.

505
00:26:52,854 --> 00:26:54,481
You could have easily hired
someone to blow up Mashburn.

506
00:26:54,606 --> 00:26:56,817
And assassinate him
at Chaparral Glen.

507
00:26:56,942 --> 00:26:57,984
But your guy failed

508
00:26:58,110 --> 00:26:59,611
so you took it up yourself
to kill him with this.

509
00:27:01,488 --> 00:27:02,989
What, Walter?

510
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:05,033
I would never hurt Walter.

511
00:27:05,408 --> 00:27:07,744
I love Walter, and he love me.

512
00:27:08,870 --> 00:27:11,790
It was you I was going to kill,
you little slut.

513
00:27:12,082 --> 00:27:14,292
- Excuse me?
- You kissed him.

514
00:27:14,417 --> 00:27:15,460
I did not.

515
00:27:16,253 --> 00:27:17,337
I didn't.

516
00:27:17,963 --> 00:27:20,090
- You were about to.
- I did not kiss him.

517
00:27:20,382 --> 00:27:21,591
None of my business.

518
00:27:22,801 --> 00:27:27,264
You are totally wrong for him.
So little and bony.

519
00:27:27,472 --> 00:27:29,432
Well, she does have
a damaged intensity

520
00:27:29,558 --> 00:27:31,476
that some people
might find attractive.

521
00:27:32,686 --> 00:27:36,606
Elsa, you've admitted to assault
with a deadly weapon on a cop.

522
00:27:37,315 --> 00:27:39,609
You could get ten years
if you don't cooperate.

523
00:27:40,443 --> 00:27:43,155
Now who did you hire and are
they still after Walter?

524
00:27:43,613 --> 00:27:47,409
Cooperate? So you can tell
Walter what a hero you are

525
00:27:47,701 --> 00:27:49,369
how you save him from me.

526
00:27:49,703 --> 00:27:51,413
And then he kiss you again, huh?

527
00:27:51,705 --> 00:27:53,707
That is what you want, bitch?

528
00:27:54,499 --> 00:27:58,545
No. Go suck your own face.
I don't cooperate.

529
00:28:06,469 --> 00:28:07,679
What are you doing?

530
00:28:09,264 --> 00:28:10,682
Getting familiar.

531
00:28:13,226 --> 00:28:15,937
You were at Walter's to watch
over him, weren't you?

532
00:28:17,022 --> 00:28:20,025
To keep him safe
from women like Lisbon.

533
00:28:23,737 --> 00:28:25,989
- Yes.
- That's okay.

534
00:28:26,990 --> 00:28:29,409
You're very well-groomed
for a crazy person.

535
00:28:30,410 --> 00:28:33,455
Not a hair out of place.
Careful, meticulous.

536
00:28:34,664 --> 00:28:37,167
You document his protection,
don't you?

537
00:28:37,334 --> 00:28:39,127
You show him
how much you love him

538
00:28:39,628 --> 00:28:42,005
and how wrong he is
to not love you back.

539
00:28:43,715 --> 00:28:47,302
You probably keep an album
somewhere. No, not an album.

540
00:28:49,221 --> 00:28:50,847
Where's her cell phone?

541
00:28:59,231 --> 00:29:01,983
So Elsa has over 300 photos
of Mashburn on her phone.

542
00:29:02,275 --> 00:29:03,818
Mashburn on his yacht

543
00:29:04,069 --> 00:29:05,695
Mashburn at a charity event

544
00:29:06,112 --> 00:29:07,864
Mashburn having lunch
with some guy

545
00:29:07,989 --> 00:29:10,784
Mashburn having drinks
with another guy. Hang on.

546
00:29:11,743 --> 00:29:13,078
Go back.

547
00:29:17,207 --> 00:29:19,793
- That's Garth Drucker.
- Yuri Bajoran's Head of Security?

548
00:29:19,918 --> 00:29:23,046
What the hell is Drucker doing having drinks
with his boss' archenemy?

549
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:28,009
Jane, do you mind?

550
00:29:28,260 --> 00:29:30,553
Uh, Rigsby told me about
Walter and Drucker.

551
00:29:31,179 --> 00:29:32,931
Mashburn's been deceiving us
from the get-go.

552
00:29:33,056 --> 00:29:36,017
Mm, yeah, it should have been obvious
that they knew each other.

553
00:29:36,351 --> 00:29:37,894
Garth Drucker's bank records.

554
00:29:38,061 --> 00:29:40,605
For the past six months he's been
receiving payments of $50,000

555
00:29:40,730 --> 00:29:43,650
from one of Mashburn's
holding companies, a payoff.

556
00:29:44,234 --> 00:29:45,944
Walter's a bad boy.
So what?

557
00:29:46,069 --> 00:29:48,321
Corporate espionage
happens all the time.

558
00:29:48,446 --> 00:29:50,240
He said he'd never been
to Yuri's company before.

559
00:29:50,365 --> 00:29:52,575
He was there a few days ago.
Drucker let him in.

560
00:29:53,076 --> 00:29:55,620
This is from security footage.
I found it at Drucker's house.

561
00:29:55,745 --> 00:29:57,247
He must have been keeping it
as insurance.

562
00:29:57,372 --> 00:29:59,874
Bottom line is, Mashburn
could've planted that bomb.

563
00:30:00,041 --> 00:30:01,334
That's a cool photo.

564
00:30:01,584 --> 00:30:03,253
- Is this funny to you?
- No, not at all.

565
00:30:03,420 --> 00:30:06,798
How do you explain the sniper, then?
Is that a mislead?

566
00:30:06,923 --> 00:30:09,384
Exactly. Mashburn makes us
think he's the target.

567
00:30:09,509 --> 00:30:11,011
He's smart.
Maybe he's that smart.

568
00:30:12,804 --> 00:30:14,472
- Tell me I'm wrong.
- You're wrong.

569
00:30:15,015 --> 00:30:17,726
- Why?
- The sniper very nearly killed you.

570
00:30:17,851 --> 00:30:19,019
Walter wouldn't let that happen

571
00:30:19,144 --> 00:30:21,730
at least I believed that
he wouldn't let that happen.

572
00:30:22,272 --> 00:30:24,899
And on the other hand,
we have the problem of motive.

573
00:30:25,525 --> 00:30:27,986
Walter made a really good case
for wanting to keep Yuri alive

574
00:30:28,111 --> 00:30:30,739
to humiliate him,
so what's his motive to kill?

575
00:30:30,864 --> 00:30:31,990
Not what...

576
00:30:33,116 --> 00:30:34,576
Who.

577
00:30:34,784 --> 00:30:37,162
- Is Walter still in love with you?
- What?

578
00:30:37,287 --> 00:30:38,747
Well, you wouldn't talk
about it before.

579
00:30:38,872 --> 00:30:41,666
It's about guilt, isn't it?
You broke his heart.

580
00:30:42,167 --> 00:30:43,793
Why does any of this
matter now?

581
00:30:43,918 --> 00:30:45,837
Please, it's important.

582
00:30:46,629 --> 00:30:49,549
Do you think Walter may have
been jealous of you and Yuri?

583
00:30:49,674 --> 00:30:51,134
Walter was different
back then.

584
00:30:52,260 --> 00:30:53,511
Sweet.

585
00:30:54,679 --> 00:30:57,682
The night I gave back his ring
and told him about Yuri

586
00:30:58,433 --> 00:31:01,144
I could see something crack
inside him.

587
00:31:02,437 --> 00:31:04,356
He spent
the next half dozen years

588
00:31:04,647 --> 00:31:07,484
dating and often marrying
the most dreadful bimbos.

589
00:31:08,777 --> 00:31:10,904
He does have questionable taste
in women.

590
00:31:11,946 --> 00:31:14,324
Some men are like that
with that first great love.

591
00:31:14,449 --> 00:31:16,785
Their... heart breaks

592
00:31:16,910 --> 00:31:20,830
and the pieces never fit back
together quite the same way.

593
00:31:21,414 --> 00:31:24,959
I'm... I'm very sorry I hurt Walter.

594
00:31:26,961 --> 00:31:28,296
We think that
there's a possibility

595
00:31:28,421 --> 00:31:30,632
that Walter may have been
involved in the bombing.

596
00:31:30,924 --> 00:31:33,718
No. No, I-I don't believe that.

597
00:31:33,843 --> 00:31:35,178
Well, it's quite simple, really.

598
00:31:35,303 --> 00:31:37,889
I mean, you stage an attack.
You appear to be the victim.

599
00:31:38,264 --> 00:31:42,227
No one suspects the victim.
You have something to add?

600
00:31:44,354 --> 00:31:47,023
That night, Walter said
he'd win me back

601
00:31:48,233 --> 00:31:50,026
no matter how long it took.

602
00:31:52,570 --> 00:31:55,949
Mrs. Bajoran, I have a plan,
but I'm gonna need your help.

603
00:31:56,074 --> 00:31:57,158
Of course.

604
00:31:57,283 --> 00:32:00,995
You're gonna confront Walter
and when he looks into your eyes

605
00:32:01,496 --> 00:32:04,040
if he did this for you,
he won't be able to hide it.

606
00:32:05,750 --> 00:32:09,421
- I wanna talk to him first.
- Well...

607
00:32:09,838 --> 00:32:14,175
Okay. Uh, she's... she's gonna
talk to him first.

608
00:32:14,676 --> 00:32:16,010
Of course you can have
the car, Markham.

609
00:32:16,136 --> 00:32:18,179
What am I gonna do
with James Dean's car?

610
00:32:18,555 --> 00:32:20,682
Yeah, I'll send the paperwork
over today.

611
00:32:20,974 --> 00:32:23,726
You make the check out
to my favorite charity, okay?

612
00:32:24,352 --> 00:32:25,520
Yeah. I gotta go.

613
00:32:26,688 --> 00:32:28,273
Teresa, a pleasure.

614
00:32:28,773 --> 00:32:30,191
Hey, I would have been happy
to come to your office.

615
00:32:30,483 --> 00:32:32,986
- Coulda watched you work.
- That would have been awkward.

616
00:32:33,236 --> 00:32:34,279
Listen, if this is
about last night...

617
00:32:34,404 --> 00:32:37,365
it would have been awkward
because I was investigating you.

618
00:32:38,366 --> 00:32:39,659
I know about you and Drucker.

619
00:32:39,784 --> 00:32:42,162
Oh, look, that was industrial
espionage, pure and simple.

620
00:32:42,287 --> 00:32:43,955
Did you kill Yuri?

621
00:32:44,330 --> 00:32:47,041
Hang on. We're back to that?
You think I did it?

622
00:32:47,459 --> 00:32:50,170
If you did, I gotta hand it
to you, it was smart.

623
00:32:50,378 --> 00:32:51,671
You sure fooled me.

624
00:32:52,338 --> 00:32:53,882
You're wrong.

625
00:32:54,007 --> 00:32:57,010
Look, Teresa, I know
you have trust issues...

626
00:32:57,135 --> 00:32:58,928
You don't know
anything about me.

627
00:32:59,053 --> 00:33:01,931
Sure, I do. You were raised in
Chicago. Your mom was a nurse.

628
00:33:02,056 --> 00:33:05,268
Your dad was a fireman. You have
three brothers... Thomas, James...

629
00:33:05,477 --> 00:33:06,895
you checked me out.

630
00:33:10,940 --> 00:33:12,108
Listen to me.

631
00:33:12,233 --> 00:33:15,778
I am this close... this close
to arresting you for murder.

632
00:33:17,197 --> 00:33:18,364
You know what?

633
00:33:18,823 --> 00:33:20,325
I'm gonna go inside.

634
00:33:20,700 --> 00:33:22,785
I'm gonna make myself
a stiff drink

635
00:33:22,911 --> 00:33:25,538
and I really hope you'll join me
so that we can talk about this.

636
00:33:25,705 --> 00:33:28,625
If you did this thing, we'll find the proof.
You know we will.

637
00:33:28,750 --> 00:33:31,294
And it's just a matter of time
before I put you away.

638
00:33:32,462 --> 00:33:34,255
I expect nothing less, Teresa.

639
00:33:41,179 --> 00:33:44,307
Hey, Lisbon.
Where's Walter going?

640
00:33:44,474 --> 00:33:47,185
- In the house.
- Perfect. I'll go get him.

641
00:33:48,269 --> 00:33:50,271
I can't believe
Walter did this.

642
00:33:52,273 --> 00:33:54,025
I'm sorry.
It's a lot to handle.

643
00:33:54,192 --> 00:33:55,818
It's all right.
You're upset.

644
00:33:57,278 --> 00:34:00,782
So are you, Miss Lisbon.
Why is that?

645
00:34:02,825 --> 00:34:04,577
Lisbon! Help!

646
00:34:11,376 --> 00:34:12,961
Jane, you all right?

647
00:34:13,086 --> 00:34:16,422
He hit me.
He hit me.

648
00:34:27,515 --> 00:34:29,100
Did Mashburn
say anything to you?

649
00:34:29,225 --> 00:34:30,518
Just that he'd never risk
going to jail

650
00:34:30,643 --> 00:34:32,353
he has a lot of money
in overseas accounts

651
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:33,604
and he'd be happy
to live there.

652
00:34:33,729 --> 00:34:35,147
Oh, except we know that
he hasn't left the country.

653
00:34:35,273 --> 00:34:36,315
We've frozen his bank accounts

654
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:37,650
and every cop in the state's
looking for him.

655
00:34:37,775 --> 00:34:39,944
Mrs. Bajoran, thank you for coming.
Why don't you have a seat?

656
00:34:40,945 --> 00:34:42,113
No sign of Walter yet?

657
00:34:42,238 --> 00:34:46,617
Just his car. We found it abandoned
a few miles from his palatial mansion.

658
00:34:46,742 --> 00:34:49,120
We'll find him. I promise.
And you can help.

659
00:34:49,453 --> 00:34:50,997
You know Mashburn
better than anybody.

660
00:34:51,163 --> 00:34:53,040
We found this
on the seat of his car.

661
00:34:53,249 --> 00:34:54,417
Do you know what it means?

662
00:34:54,584 --> 00:34:57,295
"G-F-M-C-A-1710."

663
00:34:58,921 --> 00:35:01,048
I don't know.
An address of some kind.

664
00:35:01,173 --> 00:35:02,925
- Address to where?
- I don't know.

665
00:35:04,594 --> 00:35:06,804
I'm... I'm sorry, Agent Lisbon.
It's been too long.

666
00:35:06,929 --> 00:35:10,558
I-I don't know Walter anymore.
That's obvious to me now.

667
00:35:58,356 --> 00:36:01,651
Walter! Turn around.

668
00:36:02,777 --> 00:36:03,986
I win!

669
00:36:05,237 --> 00:36:07,865
Not so much, Yuri.
No.

670
00:36:08,699 --> 00:36:11,118
Drop it, Bajoran! Now.

671
00:36:12,703 --> 00:36:14,372
Jane, you can come out now.

672
00:36:16,624 --> 00:36:18,125
Yuri Bajoran!

673
00:36:18,250 --> 00:36:21,504
You're looking delightfully
not-so-blown-up by a bomb.

674
00:36:21,879 --> 00:36:24,590
Very clever of you, I must say.
No one suspects a dead man.

675
00:36:24,715 --> 00:36:26,926
Well, almost no one.

676
00:36:27,385 --> 00:36:32,556
You staged all this... Mashburn running...
just to lure me out.

677
00:36:32,682 --> 00:36:34,684
Well, not bad
for a state employee, huh?

678
00:36:34,934 --> 00:36:37,478
Uh, consultant, really.

679
00:36:37,603 --> 00:36:39,522
Walter finally beat you.

680
00:36:40,106 --> 00:36:43,317
He was gonna take over your company
and your ego couldn't handle that.

681
00:36:43,442 --> 00:36:45,319
So you put that military experience to use.

682
00:36:45,528 --> 00:36:49,198
Kill Mashburn and Drucker, who betrayed you
then leave the country with Marie.

683
00:36:49,323 --> 00:36:51,450
But Mashburn ruined it
for you, didn't he?

684
00:36:51,951 --> 00:36:53,744
You didn't know that he used
your fake death threat

685
00:36:53,869 --> 00:36:56,914
as a reason to call in Lisbon and myself
and you were stuck.

686
00:37:00,418 --> 00:37:04,422
It was my last chance
before signing that damn contract.

687
00:37:04,922 --> 00:37:06,090
I had to do it then.

688
00:37:07,425 --> 00:37:09,593
Let's do the damn deal, Walter.

689
00:37:11,679 --> 00:37:13,681
"Oh, yeah,
and everything was in place..."

690
00:37:13,806 --> 00:37:17,435
"the bomb, and, what, a little
D.N.A. sprinkled everywhere..."

691
00:37:17,601 --> 00:37:19,478
"To prove that you died
in that explosion?"

692
00:37:19,812 --> 00:37:21,605
Hey, Teresa,
while you're here...

693
00:37:21,772 --> 00:37:23,607
"You set the timer
and got out of there."

694
00:37:23,774 --> 00:37:25,192
"You timed it
almost perfectly."

695
00:37:26,569 --> 00:37:28,237
But Walter escaped.

696
00:37:28,529 --> 00:37:30,573
And then you missed him
again in Chaparral Glen.

697
00:37:30,698 --> 00:37:32,199
Mashburn's a cockroach.

698
00:37:32,950 --> 00:37:34,493
He wouldn't die.

699
00:37:38,080 --> 00:37:41,333
Now I have a question for you, Mr. Jane.

700
00:37:44,837 --> 00:37:46,088
How did you know?

701
00:37:54,889 --> 00:37:56,140
"Yuri's toupees?"

702
00:37:56,515 --> 00:37:57,641
Yes, in his bedroom

703
00:37:57,767 --> 00:38:00,060
he had five heads
and only two toupees.

704
00:38:00,186 --> 00:38:03,189
Fine, he was wearing one.
That leaves still two missing

705
00:38:03,314 --> 00:38:06,984
and only one person would
have, uh, such a need for...

706
00:38:08,861 --> 00:38:10,613
Such a personal object.

707
00:38:11,155 --> 00:38:12,323
Yuri took them?

708
00:38:12,615 --> 00:38:17,244
Yeah. Yeah, I guess,
uh, you find a good rug

709
00:38:17,620 --> 00:38:19,955
you, uh, get
very connected to it.

710
00:38:21,499 --> 00:38:23,793
Thank you for your help
in, uh, catching him.

711
00:38:23,918 --> 00:38:26,086
- Oh. Not at all. It was fun.
- Mm. Yeah. Hmm.

712
00:38:26,212 --> 00:38:27,630
Sorry. It was your idea.

713
00:38:28,631 --> 00:38:30,800
Though I still can't believe
that Marie wanted me dead.

714
00:38:31,300 --> 00:38:33,010
You have a knack
for picking 'em.

715
00:38:34,428 --> 00:38:36,347
Almost forgot.
Your credit card.

716
00:38:36,931 --> 00:38:37,973
Thank you.

717
00:38:39,391 --> 00:38:41,894
Patrick, hang on.
One question.

718
00:38:42,561 --> 00:38:44,188
Do you think
Teresa believed it...

719
00:38:44,313 --> 00:38:45,606
that I was the killer?

720
00:38:47,066 --> 00:38:50,528
Yeah, she did for a minute there
but I wouldn't think anything of it.

721
00:39:09,213 --> 00:39:11,423
- We caught lady MacBeth?
- Yeah, at the Canadian border.

722
00:39:11,549 --> 00:39:12,716
Was just gonna come tell the boss.

723
00:39:13,259 --> 00:39:15,761
- Where is she?
- Don't know.

724
00:39:19,348 --> 00:39:21,475
- Good morning.
- Morning.

725
00:39:23,853 --> 00:39:25,729
I'm very glad
you came over last night.

726
00:39:28,023 --> 00:39:29,066
Me, too.

727
00:39:31,068 --> 00:39:33,028
I'll call room service,
order some breakfast.

728
00:39:33,153 --> 00:39:34,989
Nah, nah, I can't.
I'm late.

729
00:39:35,281 --> 00:39:37,616
What can I say?
The bastards keep killing people.

730
00:39:39,201 --> 00:39:40,744
Well, when am I
gonna see you again?

731
00:39:40,870 --> 00:39:42,079
Aren't you going
to Europe tomorrow?

732
00:39:42,204 --> 00:39:45,082
Oh. Two months.
Got board meetings.

733
00:39:45,666 --> 00:39:47,751
Well, there you go then.

734
00:40:08,188 --> 00:40:09,815
It was nice seeing you, Walter.

735
00:40:19,909 --> 00:40:22,286
Can't believe I'm a one-night stand
for Dirty Harry.

736
00:40:23,287 --> 00:40:26,582
Yeah, well, I'd leave you cab fare
but you probably got that covered, right?

737
00:40:35,549 --> 00:40:36,592
Bye, Teresa.

738
00:40:38,010 --> 00:40:39,428
Good-bye, Walter.

739
00:40:43,933 --> 00:40:45,893
Lisbon. Yeah.

740
00:40:46,518 --> 00:40:50,105
Okay, liaise with Costa Mesa P.D.
Put a lid on the crime scene.

741
00:40:50,314 --> 00:40:52,441
You and Cho start canvassing.
It's a crowded neighborhood.

742
00:40:52,566 --> 00:40:53,651
Somebody saw something.

